INSERT INTO `diagram_metadata` VALUES (262,1,'الوحدة 1: دراسة المادة','الفصل 2: المخاليط والمحاليل','الدرس 1: المحاليل والذائبية','A line graph titled \'الذائبية\' (Solubility) showing the solubility of four different substances in grams of solute per 100 grams of water as a function of temperature, with the temperature ranging from 0 to 90 degrees Celsius.','diagram_page_45_diag_01.png','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_45_diag_01.png','432x381','YES','YES','The image contains a scientific graph that illustrates the relationship between solubility and temperature, which is relevant for an 8th-grade science curriculum.','2026-11-23 07:04:12',NULL),(263,1,'الوحدة 1: دراسة المادة','الفصل 2: المخاليط والمحاليل','الدرس 2: المحاليل الحمضية والمحاليل القاعدية','The image shows a chemical equation illustrating the formation of the hydronium ion (H₃O⁺) from a hydrogen ion (H⁺) and a water molecule (H₂O). On the left, a blue sphere represents the hydrogen ion, and a red and blue sphere represents the water molecule. On the right, the hydronium ion is depicted as a combination of these two components.','diagram_page_49_diag_02.png','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_49_diag_02.png','856x301','YES','YES','The image contains a chemical equation and a molecular representation relevant to the topic of acid-base solutions.','2026-11-23 07:04:12',NULL),(264,1,'الوحدة 1: دراسة المادة','الفصل 2: المخاليط والمحاليل','الدرس 2: المحاليل الحمضية والمحاليل القاعدية','A pH scale ranging from 0 to 14, illustrating the acidity and alkalinity of various common substances. The scale indicates that values below 7 represent acidic substances, values above 7 represent alkaline substances, and 7 is neutral. Substances depicted include vinegar, lemon juice, tomato, blood, and soda, with corresponding pH values labeled.','diagram_page_53_diag_03.png','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_53_diag_03.png','1277x452','YES','YES','The image effectively illustrates the pH scale and the acidity/alkalinity of various substances, which is relevant for an 8th-grade science curriculum.','2026-11-23 07:04:12',NULL),(265,1,'الوحدة 1: دراسة المادة','الفصل 2: المخاليط والمحاليل','الدرس 2: المحاليل الحمضية والمحاليل القاعدية','The image shows two beakers. The left beaker contains hydrochloric acid with blue and yellow ions represented, while the right beaker contains ethanoic acid with purple and pink ions. Both beakers illustrate the presence of ions in the solutions.','diagram_page_54_diag_04.png','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_54_diag_04.png','758x423','YES','YES','The image effectively demonstrates the concept of strong and weak acids through visual representation of their ionic compositions.','2026-11-23 07:04:12',NULL),(266,1,'الوحدة 1: دراسة المادة','الفصل 2: المخاليط والمحاليل','الدرس 2: المحاليل الحمضية والمحاليل القاعدية','The image displays a pH scale ranging from 0 to 14, with labels indicating the dominant ionic species in aqueous solutions: H3O+ on the acidic side (pH 0-7) and OH- on the basic side (pH 7-14).','diagram_page_55_diag_05.png','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_55_diag_05.png','1060x532','YES','YES','The image effectively illustrates the pH scale and the corresponding ionic species, which is relevant for understanding acid-base chemistry.','2026-11-23 07:04:12',NULL),(267,1,'الوحدة 1: دراسة المادة','الفصل 2: المخاليط والمحاليل','استقصاء ومراجعة الفصل واختبار مقنن','A line graph titled \'الذائبية\' (Solubility) showing the relationship between temperature (°C) on the x-axis and solubility in grams per 100 grams of water on the y-axis. The graph includes two lines representing the solubility of potassium chloride and sodium chloride, with temperature ranging from 0 to 90°C in increments of 10.','diagram_page_62_diag_06.png','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_62_diag_06.png','437x297','YES','YES','The image contains a scientific graph that illustrates a key concept in chemistry related to solubility.','2026-11-23 07:04:12',NULL),(268,1,'الوحدة 1: در