ound the nucleus. The nucleus is labeled in Arabic as \'النواة\' and the particles are labeled as \'بروتون\' for protons, \'نيترون\' for neutrons, and \'إلكترونات\' for electrons.','diagram_page_129_diag_21.png','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_129_diag_21.png','568x607','YES','YES','The diagram effectively represents the atomic structure, which is relevant for an 8th-grade science curriculum.','2026-11-23 07:04:12',NULL),(283,1,'الوحدة العامة','الفصل العام','الدرس العام','A concept map illustrating the classification of matter, showing that matter is divided into four main states: solid, liquid, gas, and plasma, with additional notes on their properties regarding shape and volume.','diagram_page_129_diag_22.png','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_129_diag_22.png','652x519','YES','YES','The image presents a clear scientific diagram that categorizes matter and its states, suitable for educational purposes.','2026-11-23 07:04:12',NULL),(284,1,'الوحدة العامة','الفصل العام','الدرس العام','A Venn diagram showing the atomic arrangements of diamond and graphite. The left circle (blue) represents diamond, stating that atoms are arranged in cubic crystal form. The right circle (green) represents graphite, indicating that atoms are arranged in layers. The overlapping area identifies carbon as the common element.','diagram_page_131_diag_23.png','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_131_diag_23.png','621x301','YES','YES','The diagram effectively illustrates the atomic structures of diamond and graphite, which is relevant to 8th-grade science.','2026-11-23 07:04:12',NULL),(285,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 5: جهازا الدوران والمناعة','الدرس 1: جهاز الدوران','The image shows a magnified view of blood components, including red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. It is divided into two circular sections: the left side features a realistic microscopic image, while the right side presents a simplified, labeled diagram of the same components.','diagram_page_16_di