INSERT INTO `diagram_questions` VALUES (1,1,'الوحدة 1: دراسة المادة','الفصل 2: المخاليط والمحاليل','الدرس 1: المحاليل والذائبية','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_45_diag_01.png','YES','The graph presents distinct labeled components related to solubility, making it suitable for educational purposes and question derivation.','What is the solubility of sucrose at 90 degrees Celsius?','Approximately 480 grams of sucrose per 100 grams of water.','Which substance shows the most significant increase in solubility with temperature?','{\"A\": \"سكروز (Sucrose)\", \"B\": \"كلوريد الصوديوم (Sodium Chloride)\", \"C\": \"كلوريد البوتاسيوم (Potassium Chloride)\", \"D\": \"كربونات الكالسيوم (Calcium Carbonate)\"}','A','سكروز (Sucrose) shows a significant increase in solubility as temperature rises, as indicated by the steep curve on the graph.','Explain why the solubility of potassium chloride increases moderately with temperature.','The solubility of potassium chloride increases moderately with temperature due to the increased kinetic energy of water molecules, which allows more solute particles to dissolve. However, the increase is not as pronounced as that of sucrose, indicating that the interactions between potassium chloride and water are less affected by temperature changes compared to sucrose.','2026-11-17 13:26:54'),(2,1,'الوحدة 1: دراسة المادة','الفصل 2: المخاليط والمحاليل','الدرس 2: المحاليل الحمضية والمحاليل القاعدية','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_49_diag_02.png','YES','The illustration depicts a molecular interaction with distinct components that can be labeled and used for educational questions about chemical reactions.','What is formed when a hydrogen ion (H⁺) combines with a water molecule (H₂O)?','A hydronium ion (H₃O⁺) is formed.','What does the chemical equation H⁺ + H₂O → H₃O⁺ represent?','{\"A\": \"The formation of a hydronium ion\", \"B\": \"The dissociation of water\", \"C\": \"The formation of hydrogen gas\", \"D\": \"The reaction of acids with bases\"}','A','The equation shows that a hydrogen ion combines with a water molecule to form a hydronium ion.','Explain how a hydronium ion (H₃O⁺) is formed from a hydrogen ion (H⁺) and a water molecule (H₂O).','A hydronium ion is formed when a hydrogen ion (H⁺), which is a proton, attaches to a water molecule (H₂O). The water molecule consists of one oxygen atom and two hydrogen atoms. When the hydrogen ion combines with the water molecule, it creates a new ion, the hydronium ion (H₃O⁺), which has three hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom, resulting in a positively charged ion.','2026-11-17 13:26:54'),(3,1,'الوحدة 1: دراسة المادة','الفصل 2: المخاليط والمحاليل','الدرس 2: المحاليل الحمضية والمحاليل القاعدية','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_54_diag_03.png','YES','The illustration depicts molecular models of ionic compounds with distinct labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What type of acid is represented in the left beaker?','Hydrochloric acid (حمض الهيدروكلوريك)','Which ion is present in a higher concentration in the hydrochloric acid solution compared to the ethanoic acid solution?','{\"A\": \"Hydronium ion (أيون الهيدرونيوم)\", \"B\": \"Chloride ion (أيون الكلوريد)\", \"C\": \"Acetate ion (أيون الأسيتات)\", \"D\": \"Sodium ion (أيون الصوديوم)\"}','A','The hydrochloric acid solution has a high concentration of hydronium ions due to its strong acid nature, while the ethanoic acid solution has a lower concentration of hydronium ions.','Explain why hydrochloric acid is considered a strong acid while ethanoic acid is considered a weak acid.','Hydrochloric acid is considered a strong acid because it completely ionizes in water, resulting in a high concentration of free ions, specifically hydronium ions. In contrast, ethanoic acid only partially ionizes in water, leading to a lower concentration of free ions. This difference in ionization is what categorizes hydrochloric acid as strong and ethanoic acid as weak.','2026-11-17 13:26:54'),(4,1,'الوحدة 1: دراسة المادة','الفصل 2: المخاليط والمحاليل','الدرس 2: المحاليل الحمضية والمحاليل القاعدية','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_55_diag_04.png','YES','The illustration effectively represents the pH scale and the relationship between hydronium and hydroxide ions, which is relevant for understanding acid-base chemistry.','What is the pH range for acidic solutions?','The pH range for acidic solutions is from 0 to 7.','Which ion is dominant in acidic solutions (pH 0 to 7)?','{\"A\": \"H₃O⁺\", \"B\": \"OH⁻\", \"C\": \"Na⁺\", \"D\": \"Cl⁻\"}','A','H₃O⁺ (hydronium ion) is the dominant ion in acidic solutions, as indicated on the left side of the pH scale in the diagram.','Explain how the pH scale indicates the acidity or basicity of a solution.','The pH scale ranges from 0 to 14, where values below 7 indicate acidic solutions (higher concentration of H₃O⁺ ions), values above 7 indicate basic solutions (higher concentration of OH⁻ ions), and a value of 7 indicates a neutral solution. This scale helps in determining the nature of a solution based on its ion concentration.','2026-11-17 13:26:54'),(5,1,'الوحدة 2: المادة والطاقة','الفصل 3: حالات المادة','الدرس 1: المادة','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_72_diag_07.png','YES','The illustration depicts a molecular model with distinct labeled components (sodium and chlorine), making it suitable for educational purposes.','What is the arrangement of atoms in a crystal structure?','Atoms in a crystal structure are arranged in a three-dimensional lattice, often in a repeating unit cell.','What do the larger lime-green spheres represent in the crystal structure diagram?','{\"A\": \"Sodium ions\", \"B\": \"Chloride ions\", \"C\": \"Water molecules\", \"D\": \"Carbon atoms\"}','A','The larger lime-green spheres are labeled as الصوديوم, which translates to sodium in Arabic.','How do the smaller light gray/silver spheres fit into the crystal structure?','The smaller light gray/silver spheres occupy the octahedral voids created by the larger lime-green spheres, filling the spaces between them to maintain a stable crystal lattice structure.','2026-11-17 13:26:54'),(6,1,'الوحدة 2: المادة والطاقة','الفصل 3: حالات المادة','الدرس 1: المادة','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_72_diag_08.png','YES','The illustration depicts a molecular model with distinct components that can be labeled and used to formulate educational questions about atomic structure and interactions.','What is the primary structure shown in the diagram?','The diagram illustrates the crystal structure of a compound.','What do the larger lime-green spheres represent in the crystal structure?','{\"A\": \"Atoms or ions occupying corners and face-centered positions\", \"B\": \"Vacancies in the crystal lattice\", \"C\": \"Electrons surrounding the nucleus\", \"D\": \"Molecules of a gas\"}','A','The larger lime-green spheres represent atoms or ions that occupy the corners and face-centered positions of the unit cell in the crystal structure.','Explain how the arrangement of spheres in the crystal structure contributes to its stability.','The arrangement of spheres in a crystal structure creates a stable lattice due to the efficient packing of atoms or ions. Larger spheres occupy the corners and face-centered positions, while smaller spheres fill the octahedral voids. This close packing maximizes attractive forces between the particles, minimizing potential energy and enhancing stability. The geometric arrangement also allows for uniform distribution of forces, which contributes to the overall strength and integrity of the crystal.','2026-11-17 13:26:54'),(7,1,'الوحدة 2: المادة والطاقة','الفصل 3: حالات المادة','الدرس 1: المادة','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_72_diag_09.png','YES','The illustration depicts molecular structures that can be labeled and used to formulate educational questions about crystal formation and properties.','What is the primary structure represented in the diagram?','The primary structure represented is a crystalline lattice of a compound.','In the crystal structure diagram, where are the larger lime-green spheres located?','{\"A\": \"At the corners and face-centered positions of the unit cell\", \"B\": \"Only at the center of the unit cell\", \"C\": \"Scattered randomly throughout the structure\", \"D\": \"Only at the edges of the unit cell\"}','A','The larger lime-green spheres occupy the corners and face-centered positions of the unit cell, as described in the diagram.','Explain how the arrangement of spheres in the crystal structure contributes to its stability.','The arrangement of larger and smaller spheres in the crystal structure creates a stable lattice by maximizing the attractive forces between the spheres. The larger spheres occupy the corners and face-centered positions, while the smaller spheres fill the octahedral voids. This close packing minimizes empty space and allows for strong interactions between the atoms or ions, enhancing the overall stability of the crystal.','2026-11-17 13:26:54'),(8,1,'الوحدة 2: المادة والطاقة','الفصل 3: حالات المادة','الدرس 2: الحرارة وتحولات المادة','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_79_diag_10.png','YES','The illustration depicts laboratory apparatus, which is relevant for teaching scientific concepts related to states of matter and experiments.','What is the state of matter shown in the flask?','The state of matter shown in the flask is vapor.','What does the label \'الحالة الغازية: بخار\' indicate about the contents of the flask?','{\"A\": \"The contents are in a gaseous state as vapor.\", \"B\": \"The contents are in a solid state.\", \"C\": \"The contents are in a liquid state.\", \"D\": \"The contents are a mixture of solid and liquid.\"}','A','Option A is correct because the label explicitly states that the contents are in the gaseous state as vapor.','Explain how the appearance of the substance in the flask supports its classification as vapor.','The appearance of the substance in the flask is cloudy and occupies the upper portion, indicating it is less dense and fills the available space, which is characteristic of gases. This visual representation aligns with the definition of vapor, confirming its classification as a gaseous state.','2026-11-17 13:26:55'),(9,1,'الوحدة 2: المادة والطاقة','الفصل 3: حالات المادة','الدرس 3: سلوك الموائع','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_88_diag_11.png','YES','The illustration depicts molecular models within flasks, which can be labeled and used to explain concepts related to states of matter or chemical reactions.','What are the two forces acting on a person floating in water?','The two forces are weight (الوزن) acting downward and buoyancy force (قوة الطفو) acting upward.','What does the red downward arrow labeled \'الوزن\' represent in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"The weight of the person\", \"B\": \"The buoyancy force\", \"C\": \"The surface tension of water\", \"D\": \"The gravitational pull on the water\"}','A','The red downward arrow labeled \'الوزن\' represents the weight of the person, which acts downward due to gravity.','Explain why a person can float in water without sinking.','A person can float in water without sinking because the buoyancy force acting upward is equal to or greater than the weight acting downward. This balance of forces allows the person to remain on the surface of the water.','2026-11-17 13:26:55'),(10,1,'الوحدة 2: المادة والطاقة','الفصل 3: حالات المادة','الدرس 3: سلوك الموائع','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_91_diag_12.png','YES','The illustration is an anatomical diagram of the heart with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes and question derivation.','What is the function of the right side of the heart?','The right side of the heart receives deoxygenated blood from the body and pumps it to the lungs.','Which label indicates the flow of blood from the body to the heart?','{\"A\": \"الدم من الجسم\", \"B\": \"الدم إلى الرئتين\", \"C\": \"دم من الرئتين\", \"D\": \"الدم إلى الجسم\"}','A','The label \'الدم من الجسم\' indicates the entry of deoxygenated blood from the body into the right side of the heart.','Explain how the heart functions in the circulatory system.','The heart functions as a pump in the circulatory system. It has four chambers: the right atrium and ventricle, which receive deoxygenated blood from the body and pump it to the lungs for oxygenation, and the left atrium and ventricle, which receive oxygenated blood from the lungs and pump it to the rest of the body. This continuous cycle ensures that oxygen is delivered to tissues and carbon dioxide is removed.','2026-11-17 13:26:55'),(11,1,'الوحدة 2: المادة والطاقة','الفصل 4: الطاقة وتحولاتها','الدرس 2: تحولات الطاقة','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_113_diag_14.png','YES','The illustration depicts a scientific mechanism with distinct labeled components that can be identified and used for educational questions.','What is the primary function of a turbine in electricity generation?','The primary function of a turbine is to convert the energy from steam, water, or wind into mechanical energy by rotating its blades.','What causes the turbine blades to rotate?','{\"A\": \"High-speed flow of steam, water, or wind\", \"B\": \"Electric current\", \"C\": \"Magnetic fields\", \"D\": \"Chemical reactions\"}','A','The turbine blades rotate due to the high-speed flow of steam, water, or wind, which is indicated in the diagram.','Explain how the rotation of the turbine is connected to electricity generation.','The rotation of the turbine is connected to electricity generation through a shaft that is linked to an electric generator. As the turbine blades rotate due to the flow of steam, water, or wind, the connected shaft also rotates, which in turn drives the generator to produce electrical energy.','2026-11-17 13:26:55'),(12,1,'الوحدة 2: المادة والطاقة','الفصل 4: الطاقة وتحولاتها','الدرس 2: تحولات الطاقة','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_114_diag_15.png','YES','The illustration depicts a scientific mechanism related to energy conversion with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What type of energy is initially present in natural gas?','Chemical energy.','What is the role of the boiler in the energy transformation process?','{\"A\": \"It converts chemical energy into thermal energy.\", \"B\": \"It generates electricity directly.\", \"C\": \"It stores kinetic energy.\", \"D\": \"It cools down the steam.\"}','A','The boiler burns natural gas to convert chemical energy into thermal energy, which is then used to heat water.','Explain how thermal energy in water is converted into kinetic energy in steam.','When the boiler heats water using thermal energy derived from burning natural gas, the water turns into steam. This steam, which possesses high kinetic energy due to the heat, is then directed to the turbine, where it spins the blades, converting its kinetic energy into mechanical energy.','2026-11-17 13:26:55'),(13,1,'الوحدة 2: المادة والطاقة','الفصل 4: الطاقة وتحولاتها','الدرس 2: تحولات الطاقة','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_115_diag_16.png','YES','This pie chart effectively represents data distribution, making it suitable for educational questions related to percentages and data interpretation.','What is the total percentage represented in the pie chart?','99%','Which slice of the pie chart represents the largest percentage?','{\"A\": \"38%\", \"B\": \"23%\", \"C\": \"16%\", \"D\": \"10%\"}','A','The dark red slice represents the largest percentage at 38%.','Explain how the percentages in the pie chart contribute to understanding energy transformations.','The percentages in the pie chart illustrate the distribution of different forms of energy or energy sources, helping to visualize how energy is transformed and utilized. By analyzing these proportions, one can identify which energy sources are most prevalent and how they contribute to overall energy consumption, thus providing insights into efficiency and sustainability in energy use.','2026-11-17 13:26:55'),(14,1,'الوحدة العامة','الفصل العام','الدرس العام','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_126_diag_19.png','YES','The graph represents a scientific relationship with labeled axes, making it suitable for educational purposes and question derivation.','What does the y-axis of the graph represent?','The y-axis represents Potential Energy in Joules.','At what x-axis value does the potential energy reach its maximum?','{\"A\": \"20\", \"B\": \"15\", \"C\": \"10\", \"D\": \"25\"}','A','The potential energy reaches its maximum value of approximately 15 Joules just before the x-axis value of 20.','Explain how the potential energy changes as the x-axis value increases.','As the x-axis value increases from 0, the potential energy initially increases, reaching a peak of approximately 15 Joules around the x-axis value of 19-20. After this peak, the potential energy decreases back to 0 as the x-axis value continues to increase, indicating a parabolic relationship between the two variables.','2026-11-17 13:26:55'),(15,1,'الوحدة العامة','الفصل العام','الدرس العام','output_diagrams_sem1/diagram_page_129_diag_20.png','YES','The illustration depicts a labeled atomic structure, including protons, neutrons, and electrons, which is essential for understanding basic atomic theory.','What are the two types of particles found in the nucleus of an atom?','Protons and neutrons.','What charge do protons carry in an atom?','{\"A\": \"Positive\", \"B\": \"Negative\", \"C\": \"Neutral\", \"D\": \"Variable\"}','A','Protons carry a positive charge, as indicated by the \'+\' sign in the diagram.','Explain how the arrangement of electrons affects the chemical properties of an atom.','The arrangement of electrons in different energy levels or shells determines how an atom interacts with other atoms. Atoms with similar electron configurations tend to exhibit similar chemical properties, as they have similar tendencies to gain, lose, or share electrons during chemical reactions.','2026-11-17 13:26:55'),(16,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 5: جهازا الدوران والمناعة','الدرس 1: جهاز الدوران','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_16_diag_01.png','YES','The illustration depicts blood cells with distinct labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes and question derivation.','What are the three main components of blood shown in the diagram?','The three main components of blood are red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets.','Which type of blood cell is depicted as biconcave discs in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Red blood cells\", \"B\": \"White blood cells\", \"C\": \"Platelets\", \"D\": \"Plasma\"}','A','Red blood cells are shown as numerous red, biconcave discs in the diagram, distinguishing them from the other components.','Explain the role of white blood cells in the blood.','White blood cells are crucial for the immune system as they help defend the body against infections and foreign invaders. They identify and destroy pathogens, such as bacteria and viruses, and play a key role in the body\'s immune response.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(17,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 5: جهازا الدوران والمناعة','الدرس 1: جهاز الدوران','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_19_diag_02.png','YES','The illustration depicts the human circulatory system with distinct labeled components that can be identified and used for educational purposes.','What are the two main types of blood vessels in the human circulatory system?','The two main types of blood vessels are arteries and veins.','What color represents arteries in the circulatory system diagram?','{\"A\": \"Red\", \"B\": \"Blue\", \"C\": \"Green\", \"D\": \"Yellow\"}','A','Arteries are represented in red in the circulatory system diagram, indicating that they carry oxygenated blood away from the heart.','Explain how the circulatory system functions in transporting blood throughout the body.','The circulatory system functions by using the heart to pump blood through a network of arteries and veins. Arteries carry oxygen-rich blood away from the heart to the body\'s tissues, while veins return oxygen-poor blood back to the heart. This continuous cycle ensures that all body cells receive the oxygen and nutrients they need while removing waste products.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(18,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 5: جهازا الدوران والمناعة','الدرس 1: جهاز الدوران','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_20_diag_03.png','YES','The illustration is an anatomical diagram of the respiratory system with distinct labeled components that can be identified and used for educational questions.','What is the function of the left ventricle in the human circulatory system?','The left ventricle pumps oxygenated blood to the rest of the body.','Which blood vessel carries deoxygenated blood from the lower body to the right atrium?','{\"A\": \"وريد أجوف سفلي (Inferior Vena Cava)\", \"B\": \"الأبهر (Aorta)\", \"C\": \"وريد أجوف علوي (Superior Vena Cava)\", \"D\": \"شريان رئوي (Pulmonary Artery)\"}','A','The Inferior Vena Cava carries deoxygenated blood from the lower body to the right atrium, as indicated in the diagram.','Explain how oxygenated and deoxygenated blood are distinguished in the circulatory system.','Oxygenated blood is typically represented in red and flows from the lungs to the left atrium and then to the left ventricle, which pumps it to the body. Deoxygenated blood is represented in blue and flows from the body to the right atrium via the superior and inferior vena cavae, then to the right ventricle, which sends it to the lungs for oxygenation.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(19,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 5: جهازا الدوران والمناعة','الدرس 2: المناعة والمرض','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_25_diag_04.png','YES','The illustration depicts cellular components and interactions relevant to the immune response, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What is the role of B-cells in the adaptive immune response?','B-cells produce antibodies that help neutralize pathogens.','What is the first step in the adaptive immune response as shown in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Identification of the pathogen\", \"B\": \"Activation of B-cells\", \"C\": \"Production of antibodies\", \"D\": \"Destruction of pathogens\"}','A','The diagram illustrates that the first step involves white blood cells identifying and engulfing the pathogen.','Explain how helper T-cells assist in the adaptive immune response.','Helper T-cells are activated by the identification of pathogens and play a crucial role in signaling B-cells to produce antibodies. This process enhances the immune response by ensuring that B-cells are effectively activated to target specific pathogens.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(20,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 6: الهضم والتنفس والإخراج','الدرس 1: الجهاز الهضمي والمواد الغذائية','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_46_diag_06.png','YES','The illustration clearly depicts the human digestive system with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What is the function of the liver in the digestive system?','The liver processes nutrients from the digestive tract and produces bile to aid in digestion.','Which organ is responsible for producing bile?','{\"A\": \"كبد (Kibid)\", \"B\": \"معدة (Mi\'dah)\", \"C\": \"مريء (Marii\')\", \"D\": \"غدد لعابية (Ghudud Lu\'abiyah)\"}','A','The liver (كبد) is responsible for producing bile, which helps in the digestion of fats.','Explain how the digestive system processes food after it is chewed.','After food is chewed by the teeth and mixed with saliva from the salivary glands, it forms a bolus that is swallowed. The bolus travels down the esophagus (مريء) to the stomach (معدة), where it is mixed with gastric juices for further digestion. Nutrients are then absorbed in the small intestine (أمعاء دقيقة) before waste is passed to the large intestine (أمعاء غليظة) and eventually expelled through the anus (فتحة شرج).','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(21,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 6: الهضم والتنفس والإخراج','الدرس 1: الجهاز الهضمي والمواد الغذائية','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_47_diag_07.png','YES','The illustration depicts anatomical structures of the mouth with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What is the primary function of salivary glands in the human mouth?','The primary function of salivary glands is to produce saliva, which aids in digestion and keeps the mouth moist.','How much saliva do the salivary glands produce daily?','{\"A\": \"1.5 liters\", \"B\": \"2 liters\", \"C\": \"0.5 liters\", \"D\": \"3 liters\"}','A','The diagram indicates that salivary glands produce approximately 1.5 liters of saliva daily.','Explain the role of saliva in the digestive process.','Saliva plays a crucial role in the digestive process by moistening food, which makes it easier to chew and swallow. It contains enzymes that begin the breakdown of carbohydrates, aiding in digestion. Additionally, saliva helps to neutralize acids in the mouth and provides antibacterial properties to protect oral health.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(22,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 6: الهضم والتنفس والإخراج','الدرس 1: الجهاز الهضمي والمواد الغذائية','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_48_diag_08.png','YES','The illustration depicts anatomical structures of blood vessels with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What is the primary function of the villi in the small intestine?','The primary function of the villi is to increase the surface area for absorption of nutrients.','What do the red and blue colors in the villus represent?','{\"A\": \"Arterial and venous capillaries\", \"B\": \"Lymphatic vessels\", \"C\": \"Nerve endings\", \"D\": \"Muscle fibers\"}','A','The red color represents arterial capillaries and the blue color represents venous capillaries within the villus.','Explain how the structure of the villi enhances nutrient absorption in the small intestine.','The structure of the villi enhances nutrient absorption by providing a large surface area due to their folds and projections. This allows for more contact with the digested food, facilitating the absorption of nutrients into the blood capillaries and lymphatic vessels. Additionally, the presence of capillaries and lacteals within the villi ensures efficient transport of absorbed nutrients into the bloodstream and lymphatic system.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(23,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 6: الهضم والتنفس والإخراج','الدرس 1: الجهاز الهضمي والمواد الغذائية','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_51_diag_09.png','YES','The illustration depicts a cellular structure with distinct labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What are adipocytes primarily responsible for storing?','Adipocytes are primarily responsible for storing fat.','What does the label \'دهون مختزنة\' indicate in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Stored fat\", \"B\": \"Cytoplasm\", \"C\": \"Nucleus\", \"D\": \"Interstitial tissue\"}','A','\'دهون مختزنة\' translates to \'Stored fat\', which refers to the large, clear areas within the adipocytes that represent lipid droplets.','Explain why adipocytes have a flattened nucleus.','Adipocytes have a flattened nucleus because the large fat droplet occupies most of the cell\'s interior, pushing the nucleus to the periphery. This adaptation allows for maximum storage of fat within the cell.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(24,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 6: الهضم والتنفس والإخراج','الدرس 2: جهازا التنفس والإخراج','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_58_diag_10.png','YES','The illustration depicts a red blood cell with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What is the primary function of the alveolus in the respiratory system?','The primary function of the alveolus is to facilitate gas exchange, allowing oxygen to enter the blood and carbon dioxide to be expelled from it.','What gas is indicated by the arrow moving from the alveolus into the capillary?','{\"A\": \"Oxygen (O2)\", \"B\": \"Carbon Dioxide (CO2)\", \"C\": \"Nitrogen (N2)\", \"D\": \"Hydrogen (H2)\"}','A','The arrow pointing from the alveolus into the capillary indicates the movement of oxygen (O2) from the alveolus to the red blood cells.','Explain the significance of gas exchange in the alveoli for human respiration.','Gas exchange in the alveoli is crucial for human respiration as it allows oxygen to diffuse into the bloodstream, where it is transported to cells for energy production. Simultaneously, carbon dioxide, a waste product of cellular respiration, diffuses from the blood into the alveoli to be exhaled. This process maintains the body\'s oxygen levels and removes carbon dioxide, ensuring proper cellular function.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(25,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 6: الهضم والتنفس والإخراج','الدرس 2: جهازا التنفس والإخراج','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_59_diag_11.png','YES','The illustration depicts the lungs with clear directional arrows indicating airflow, making it suitable for labeling and generating educational questions.','What is the role of the diaphragm during inhalation?','The diaphragm contracts and moves downward, increasing the thoracic cavity volume and allowing air to enter the lungs.','Which structure is indicated by the downward-pointing blue arrow on the diaphragm in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Diaphragm contraction\", \"B\": \"Air exiting the lungs\", \"C\": \"Air entering the trachea\", \"D\": \"Lung expansion\"}','A','The downward-pointing blue arrow on the diaphragm indicates that it contracts during inhalation, which is essential for drawing air into the lungs.','Explain how the process of inhalation affects the pressure inside the thoracic cavity.','During inhalation, the diaphragm contracts and moves downward, which increases the volume of the thoracic cavity. According to Boyle\'s Law, when the volume of a container increases, the pressure inside decreases. This drop in pressure allows air to flow into the lungs as it moves from an area of higher pressure (outside the body) to an area of lower pressure (inside the thoracic cavity).','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(26,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 6: الهضم والتنفس والإخراج','الدرس 2: جهازا التنفس والإخراج','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_59_diag_12.png','YES','The illustration depicts the lungs with clear directional arrows indicating airflow, making it suitable for labeling and generating educational questions.','What is the function of the diaphragm during inhalation?','The diaphragm contracts and moves downward, increasing the thoracic cavity volume and allowing air to enter the lungs.','Which structure is responsible for the movement of air into the lungs during inhalation?','{\"A\": \"Diaphragm\", \"B\": \"Trachea\", \"C\": \"Bronchi\", \"D\": \"Alveoli\"}','A','The diaphragm contracts and moves downward, creating a vacuum that pulls air into the lungs.','Explain how the diaphragm\'s movement affects the pressure in the thoracic cavity during inhalation.','When the diaphragm contracts and moves downward, it increases the volume of the thoracic cavity. According to Boyle\'s Law, as the volume increases, the pressure inside the cavity decreases. This lower pressure allows air to flow into the lungs from the higher atmospheric pressure outside the body.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(27,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 6: الهضم والتنفس والإخراج','الدرس 2: جهازا التنفس والإخراج','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_62_diag_13.png','YES','The illustration depicts the human digestive system with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What is the function of the kidneys in the human body?','The kidneys filter waste products from the blood and produce urine.','Which organ is labeled as \'المثانة\' in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Urinary bladder\", \"B\": \"Pancreas\", \"C\": \"Larynx\", \"D\": \"Esophagus\"}','A','\'المثانة\' translates to \'urinary bladder\', which is the correct answer.','Explain how the digestive system and excretory system are connected in the human body.','The digestive system breaks down food into nutrients, which are absorbed into the bloodstream. The excretory system, including the kidneys, filters out waste products from the blood, including those derived from the digestion of food, and excretes them as urine. This connection ensures that the body maintains a balance of nutrients and eliminates waste effectively.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(28,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 6: الهضم والتنفس والإخراج','الدرس 2: جهازا التنفس والإخراج','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_64_diag_14.png','YES','The illustration is an anatomical diagram of the urinary system with distinct labeled components that can be identified by students.','What are the main organs of the human urinary system?','The main organs of the human urinary system are the kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra.','Which blood vessel carries blood away from the kidneys?','{\"A\": \"Renal Vein\", \"B\": \"Renal Artery\", \"C\": \"Aorta\", \"D\": \"Ureter\"}','B','The renal artery carries oxygenated blood away from the aorta to the kidneys.','Explain the role of the kidneys in the urinary system.','The kidneys filter waste products and excess substances from the blood, producing urine. They also help regulate blood pressure, electrolyte balance, and red blood cell production.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(29,2,'الوحدة 3: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (1)','الفصل 6: الهضم والتنفس والإخراج','الدرس 2: جهازا التنفس والإخراج','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_65_diag_15.png','YES','The illustration depicts the anatomy of the kidney and its components, which are essential for understanding renal function in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What is the outer region of the kidney called?','The outer region of the kidney is called the cortex (القشرة).','What is the primary function of the nephron?','{\"A\": \"To filter blood and produce urine\", \"B\": \"To transport oxygen\", \"C\": \"To regulate body temperature\", \"D\": \"To digest food\"}','A','The nephron is the functional unit of the kidney responsible for filtering blood and producing urine.','Explain how the structure of the nephron contributes to its function in the kidney.','The nephron\'s structure, which includes components like the glomerulus and tubules, allows for efficient filtration of blood. The glomerulus filters out waste and excess substances, while the tubules reabsorb necessary nutrients and water back into the bloodstream, ensuring that waste is excreted as urine while maintaining fluid balance.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(30,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 7: أجهزة الدعامة والحركة والاستجابة','الدرس 1: الجلد والعضلات','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_85_diag_17.png','YES','The illustration is an anatomical diagram of skin layers and structures, clearly labeled for educational purposes.','What is the outermost layer of the skin called?','The outermost layer of the skin is called the epidermis (البشرة).','Which structure is responsible for producing sebum in the skin?','{\"A\": \"Sebaceous Glands (غدد دهنية)\", \"B\": \"Sweat Glands (غدد عرقية)\", \"C\": \"Hair Follicle (بصيلة الشعر)\", \"D\": \"Epidermis (البشرة)\"}','A','Sebaceous glands are specifically responsible for secreting sebum, which lubricates the skin and hair.','Explain the role of the dermis in the skin structure.','The dermis is the layer of skin located beneath the epidermis. It contains essential structures such as blood vessels, nerve endings, and glands (both sebaceous and sweat). These components play crucial roles in thermoregulation, sensation, and the overall health of the skin. The dermis also provides strength and elasticity to the skin due to its collagen and elastin fibers.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(31,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 7: أجهزة الدعامة والحركة والاستجابة','الدرس 2: الجهاز الهيكلي والجهاز العصبي','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_94_diag_18.png','YES','The illustration depicts anatomical structures of bone with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What is the function of the periosteum in a long bone?','The periosteum serves as a protective fibrous membrane covering the outer surface of the bone and provides a surface for muscle attachment.','Which part of the bone is responsible for housing bone marrow?','{\"A\": \"Medullary Cavity\", \"B\": \"Compact Bone\", \"C\": \"Spongy Bone\", \"D\": \"Periosteum\"}','A','The medullary cavity is the central cavity within the bone that contains bone marrow.','Explain how the structure of spongy bone contributes to its function.','Spongy bone has a porous, lattice-like structure that reduces the weight of the bone while maintaining strength. This design allows for the storage of bone marrow and provides space for blood vessels, facilitating nutrient and waste exchange.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(32,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 7: أجهزة الدعامة والحركة والاستجابة','الدرس 2: الجهاز الهيكلي والجهاز العصبي','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_95_diag_19.png','YES','The illustration depicts anatomical structures of bone with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What is the first stage of endochondral ossification?','The first stage is represented by cartilage, labeled as \'غضروف\' (ghadharoof).','What does the term \'مصدر دم\' (masdar dam) refer to in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Blood source\", \"B\": \"Bone structure\", \"C\": \"Cartilage\", \"D\": \"Ossification process\"}','A','\'مصدر دم\' translates to \'blood source\', indicating the importance of blood supply in the ossification process.','Explain the significance of blood vessels in the process of endochondral ossification.','Blood vessels provide essential nutrients and oxygen to the developing bone tissue. They also deliver cells that are crucial for the transformation of cartilage into bone, facilitating the ossification process.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(33,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 7: أجهزة الدعامة والحركة والاستجابة','الدرس 2: الجهاز الهيكلي والجهاز العصبي','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_98_diag_20.png','YES','The illustration depicts the human spine with distinct components that can be labeled and used for educational questions.','What is the primary function of the human skeletal system?','The primary function of the human skeletal system is to provide support, protect internal organs, and facilitate movement.','Which part of the human body is primarily represented in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Spine\", \"B\": \"Ribcage\", \"C\": \"Skull\", \"D\": \"Pelvis\"}','A','The diagram prominently displays the vertebral column, which is commonly referred to as the spine.','Explain how the skeletal system interacts with the muscular system to facilitate movement.','The skeletal system provides the framework and structure for the body, while the muscular system is responsible for movement. Muscles are attached to bones via tendons, and when muscles contract, they pull on the bones, causing movement at the joints. This interaction allows for a wide range of motions and activities.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(34,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 7: أجهزة الدعامة والحركة والاستجابة','الدرس 2: الجهاز الهيكلي والجهاز العصبي','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_100_diag_21.png','YES','The illustration depicts the structure of neurons with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What are the main components of a neuron?','The main components of a neuron are the cell body, dendrites, and axon.','What is the direction of the neural impulse in a neuron?','{\"A\": \"From the cell body along the axon towards the axon terminal\", \"B\": \"From the axon terminal to the cell body\", \"C\": \"Between dendrites only\", \"D\": \"In all directions from the cell body\"}','A','The neural impulse travels from the cell body along the axon towards the axon terminal, as indicated by the arrow in the diagram.','Explain the role of neurotransmitters in the synapse.','Neurotransmitters are chemical messengers that are released from the axon terminal into the synapse. They bind to receptors on the target cell, facilitating communication between neurons or between a neuron and a target cell. This process is crucial for transmitting signals across the synapse and enabling various functions in the nervous system.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(35,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 7: أجهزة الدعامة والحركة والاستجابة','الدرس 2: الجهاز الهيكلي والجهاز العصبي','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_101_diag_22.png','YES','The illustration depicts the human nervous system with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What are the two main parts of the human nervous system depicted in the diagram?','The central nervous system (brain and spinal cord) and the peripheral nervous system (spinal nerves).','Which structure is indicated by the label \'حبل شوكي\' in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Spinal Cord\", \"B\": \"Brain\", \"C\": \"Spinal Nerves\", \"D\": \"Peripheral Nerves\"}','A','The label \'حبل شوكي\' translates to \'spinal cord\', which is the long yellow structure extending from the brain.','Explain how the spinal nerves function in relation to the spinal cord.','Spinal nerves branch out from the spinal cord and extend to various parts of the body, allowing for communication between the central nervous system and peripheral body parts. They transmit sensory information to the spinal cord and motor commands from the spinal cord to the muscles.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(36,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 7: أجهزة الدعامة والحركة والاستجابة','الدرس 2: الجهاز الهيكلي والجهاز العصبي','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_103_diag_23.png','YES','The illustration is an anatomical diagram of the eye with distinct labeled components that can be identified and used for educational questions.','What is the function of the cornea in the human eye?','The cornea acts as the transparent outer layer that helps to focus light entering the eye.','Which part of the eye is responsible for carrying visual information to the brain?','{\"A\": \"العصب البصري (Optic Nerve)\", \"B\": \"الشبكية (Retina)\", \"C\": \"العدسة (Lens)\", \"D\": \"القزحية (Iris)\"}','A','The optic nerve (العصب البصري) is responsible for transmitting visual information from the retina to the brain.','Explain how light is processed in the human eye.','Light enters the eye through the cornea, which bends the light rays. It then passes through the pupil, controlled by the iris, and is further focused by the lens onto the retina. The retina converts the light into electrical signals that are sent to the brain via the optic nerve, allowing us to perceive images.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(37,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 7: أجهزة الدعامة والحركة والاستجابة','الدرس 2: الجهاز الهيكلي والجهاز العصبي','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_104_diag_24.png','YES','The illustration is an anatomical diagram of the ear with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What are the three main parts of the human ear?','The three main parts of the human ear are the outer ear, middle ear, and inner ear.','Which part of the ear contains the eardrum?','{\"A\": \"Middle Ear\", \"B\": \"Outer Ear\", \"C\": \"Inner Ear\", \"D\": \"Auditory Canal\"}','A','The eardrum is located in the middle ear, separating it from the outer ear.','Explain the role of the ossicles in the middle ear.','The ossicles, which include the malleus, incus, and stapes, amplify sound vibrations from the eardrum and transmit them to the inner ear. This amplification is crucial for converting sound waves into signals that can be interpreted by the brain.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(38,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 7: أجهزة الدعامة والحركة والاستجابة','الدرس 2: الجهاز الهيكلي والجهاز العصبي','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_106_diag_25.png','YES','The illustration depicts a labeled anatomical structure, which is suitable for educational purposes and can facilitate questions about its components.','What is the function of the taste pore in a taste bud?','The taste pore allows dissolved substances to enter the taste bud for taste sensation.','Which part of the taste bud contains the sensory cells responsible for taste?','{\"A\": \"خلايا حسية\", \"B\": \"خلايا داعمة\", \"C\": \"شعيرات ذوقية\", \"D\": \"ثقب ذوقي\"}','A','خلايا حسية (Sensory cells) are the receptor cells that detect taste stimuli.','Explain how the structure of taste hairs contributes to the function of taste buds.','Taste hairs, or شعيرات ذوقية, extend into the taste pore and increase the surface area for interaction with dissolved substances, enhancing the ability of sensory cells to detect different tastes.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(39,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_120_diag_27.png','YES','The graph presents distinct data points related to blood sugar levels, which can be labeled and used for educational questions.','What is the blood sugar level of a diabetic patient at 0 hours after breakfast?','Approximately 1.9 grams/liter.','At what time after breakfast does the blood sugar level of a diabetic patient peak?','{\"A\": \"1 hour\", \"B\": \"2 hours\", \"C\": \"3 hours\", \"D\": \"4 hours\"}','A','The blood sugar level of a diabetic patient peaks at approximately 2.5 grams/liter at 1 hour after breakfast.','Explain how the blood sugar levels of a healthy individual differ from those of a diabetic patient after breakfast.','After breakfast, a healthy individual\'s blood sugar levels rise moderately and stabilize, while a diabetic patient\'s levels peak significantly and then drop sharply, indicating their body\'s difficulty in regulating blood sugar.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(40,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_121_diag_28.png','YES','The illustration depicts anatomical structures of the brain with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What are the two endocrine glands shown in the diagram of the human brain?','The two endocrine glands are the Pituitary Gland (الغدة النخامية) and the Pineal Gland (الغدة الصنوبرية).','Which gland is located inferior to the thalamus and anterior to the brainstem?','{\"A\": \"Pituitary Gland\", \"B\": \"Pineal Gland\", \"C\": \"Cerebellum\", \"D\": \"Cerebrum\"}','A','The Pituitary Gland is positioned inferior to the thalamus and anterior to the brainstem, as indicated in the diagram.','Explain the role of the pituitary gland in the endocrine system.','The pituitary gland, often referred to as the \'master gland\', plays a crucial role in the endocrine system by regulating various hormones that control growth, metabolism, and reproductive functions. It releases hormones that influence other glands, such as the thyroid and adrenal glands, thereby coordinating the body\'s hormonal balance.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(41,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_121_diag_29.png','YES','The illustration depicts anatomical structures (ovaries) with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What is the function of the pituitary gland?','The pituitary gland regulates various hormonal functions and controls other endocrine glands.','Which gland is located inferior to the thalamus and anterior to the brainstem?','{\"A\": \"Pituitary Gland\", \"B\": \"Pineal Gland\", \"C\": \"Thyroid Gland\", \"D\": \"Adrenal Gland\"}','A','The pituitary gland is specifically located inferior to the thalamus and anterior to the brainstem, as shown in the diagram.','Explain the role of the pineal gland in the human body.','The pineal gland produces melatonin, a hormone that regulates sleep-wake cycles and circadian rhythms. It responds to light exposure, helping to control the body\'s internal clock.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(42,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_122_diag_30.png','YES','The illustration depicts the thyroid gland with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What are the two main glands depicted in the diagram of the human endocrine system?','The thyroid gland and the parathyroid glands.','What does the yellow line in the diagram point to?','{\"A\": \"Thyroid gland\", \"B\": \"Parathyroid gland\", \"C\": \"Larynx\", \"D\": \"Trachea\"}','B','The yellow line points to the parathyroid gland, which is labeled in Arabic as \'الغدة جارة الدرقية (خلف)\'.','Explain the anatomical relationship between the thyroid and parathyroid glands as shown in the diagram.','The thyroid gland is depicted as two reddish-orange lobed structures located on either side of the trachea, while the parathyroid glands are smaller blue-purple structures located on the posterior surface of the thyroid glands. This anatomical arrangement indicates that the parathyroid glands are situated behind the thyroid gland, which is essential for their function in regulating calcium levels in the body.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(43,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_122_diag_31.png','YES','The illustration depicts a labeled anatomical diagram of the kidney, which is suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What are the two main glands depicted in the human endocrine system diagram?','The thyroid gland and the parathyroid glands.','What does the yellow line in the diagram point to?','{\"A\": \"Thyroid gland\", \"B\": \"Parathyroid gland\", \"C\": \"Larynx\", \"D\": \"Trachea\"}','B','The yellow line points to the parathyroid gland, which is identified by the Arabic text next to it.','Explain the role of the thyroid and parathyroid glands in the endocrine system.','The thyroid gland produces hormones that regulate metabolism, growth, and development, while the parathyroid glands regulate calcium levels in the blood through the secretion of parathyroid hormone. Together, they maintain essential bodily functions and homeostasis.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(44,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_122_diag_32.png','YES','The illustration depicts the pancreas with a labeled component, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What are the main functions of the thyroid gland?','The thyroid gland regulates metabolism, growth, and development by producing hormones such as thyroxine (T4) and triiodothyronine (T3).','Which structure is identified as the parathyroid gland in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"The blue-purple spherical structures\", \"B\": \"The reddish-orange lobed structures\", \"C\": \"The light-colored cartilaginous structure\", \"D\": \"The yellow line pointing to the thyroid gland\"}','A','The blue-purple spherical structures are labeled as the parathyroid glands, indicating their location behind the thyroid gland.','Explain the relationship between the thyroid and parathyroid glands in the endocrine system.','The thyroid and parathyroid glands are closely related in the endocrine system, with the parathyroid glands located on the posterior surface of the thyroid gland. While the thyroid gland primarily regulates metabolism through hormone production, the parathyroid glands are responsible for regulating calcium levels in the blood by secreting parathyroid hormone (PTH). This relationship is crucial for maintaining homeostasis in the body.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(45,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_122_diag_33.png','YES','The illustration depicts the thyroid gland with distinct labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What are the two main glands depicted in the diagram of the human endocrine system?','The thyroid gland and the parathyroid glands.','Which gland is identified by the label \'الغدة جارة الدرقية (خلف)\' in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Parathyroid gland\", \"B\": \"Thyroid gland\", \"C\": \"Adrenal gland\", \"D\": \"Pituitary gland\"}','A','The label translates to \'Parathyroid gland (posterior)\', indicating that it refers to the parathyroid gland.','Explain the anatomical relationship between the thyroid gland and the parathyroid glands as shown in the diagram.','The thyroid gland is depicted as a larger, reddish-orange structure located around the trachea, while the parathyroid glands are shown as smaller, blue-purple structures situated on the posterior surface of the thyroid gland. This anatomical arrangement highlights the close proximity of these glands, which play important roles in regulating metabolism and calcium levels in the body.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(46,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_122_diag_34.png','YES','The illustration depicts a biological structure that can be labeled and used for educational questions related to anatomy.','What are the two main glands depicted in the diagram of the human endocrine system?','The thyroid gland and the parathyroid glands.','What does the yellow line in the diagram indicate?','{\"A\": \"Thyroid gland\", \"B\": \"Parathyroid gland (posterior)\", \"C\": \"Larynx\", \"D\": \"Trachea\"}','B','The yellow line points to the parathyroid gland, which is labeled as \'الغدة جارة الدرقية (خلف)\' in the diagram.','Explain the role of the thyroid and parathyroid glands in the human body.','The thyroid gland produces hormones that regulate metabolism, energy levels, and growth. The parathyroid glands regulate calcium levels in the blood by producing parathyroid hormone, which increases calcium absorption in the intestines and reabsorption in the kidneys, and releases calcium from bones when needed.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(47,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_123_diag_35.png','YES','The illustration depicts the process of glucose regulation in the body with distinct labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What hormone does the pancreas produce in response to high blood sugar levels?','Insulin','What is the first step in the process of regulating blood sugar levels?','{\"A\": \"Meals are eaten\", \"B\": \"Insulin is released\", \"C\": \"Blood sugar level increases\", \"D\": \"Glucose is absorbed by the intestines\"}','A','The process begins with the consumption of food, which is the first step in regulating blood sugar levels.','Explain how insulin helps to regulate blood sugar levels in the body.','Insulin helps to regulate blood sugar levels by facilitating the uptake of glucose into the liver and other tissues. When blood sugar levels rise after eating, the pancreas releases insulin, which acts like a key to allow glucose to enter cells, thereby lowering blood sugar levels back to normal.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(48,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_125_diag_36.png','YES','The illustration depicts anatomical structures related to the male reproductive system with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What are the three main parts of a sperm cell?','The three main parts of a sperm cell are the head (الرأس), nucleus (النواة), and tail (الذيل).','Which organ is responsible for storing urine in the male reproductive system?','{\"A\": \"المثانة (Bladder)\", \"B\": \"الحوصلة المنوية (Seminal Vesicle)\", \"C\": \"غدة البروستات (Prostate Gland)\", \"D\": \"القناة المنوية (Vas Deferens)\"}','A','The المثانة (Bladder) is the organ responsible for storing urine.','Explain the role of the tail (الذيل) in a sperm cell.','The tail (الذيل) of a sperm cell is crucial for its motility. It propels the sperm forward, allowing it to swim through the female reproductive tract to reach and fertilize the egg. The whip-like motion of the tail is essential for the sperm\'s ability to navigate and reach its destination.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(49,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_126_diag_37.png','YES','The illustration provides clear anatomical diagrams of the female reproductive system with labeled components that are suitable for educational purposes.','What is the function of the uterus in the female reproductive system?','The uterus is responsible for housing and nourishing a developing fetus during pregnancy.','Which organ is located anterior to the uterus in the female reproductive system?','{\"A\": \"Bladder\", \"B\": \"Ovary\", \"C\": \"Cervix\", \"D\": \"Fallopian Tube\"}','A','The bladder is positioned anterior to the uterus, as shown in the lateral view of the diagram.','Explain the role of the fallopian tubes in the female reproductive system.','The fallopian tubes transport the ova from the ovaries to the uterus. They are also the site where fertilization typically occurs when a sperm meets an egg.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(50,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 1: جهازا الغدد الصم والتكاثر','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_128_diag_38.png','YES','The illustration depicts anatomical structures with distinct labeled components that are relevant for educational purposes.','What is the duration of a typical menstrual cycle as shown in the diagram?','28 days','During which phase does menstruation occur according to the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Phase One (الطور الأول)\", \"B\": \"Phase Two (الطور الثاني)\", \"C\": \"Phase Three (الطور الثالث)\", \"D\": \"None of the above\"}','A','Menstruation occurs during Phase One (الطور الأول), specifically from days 1 to 4.','Explain how the thickness of the uterine lining changes throughout the menstrual cycle.','The thickness of the uterine lining increases during Phase Two (days 7 to 14) due to hormonal stimulation, preparing for potential implantation of an embryo. It then decreases during Phase Three (days 15 to 28) if fertilization does not occur, leading to menstruation at the start of Phase One.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(51,2,'الوحدة 4: أجهزة جسم الإنسان (2)','الفصل 8: التنظيم والتكاثر','الدرس 2: مراحل حياة الإنسان','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_134_diag_39.png','YES','The illustration depicts anatomical structures related to the female reproductive system with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What is the function of the fallopian tube in the female reproductive system?','The fallopian tube transports the egg from the ovary to the uterus and is the site where fertilization occurs.','Where does fertilization of the egg occur?','{\"A\": \"In the fallopian tube\", \"B\": \"In the ovary\", \"C\": \"In the uterus\", \"D\": \"In the cervix\"}','A','Fertilization occurs in the fallopian tube where the sperm meets the egg.','Explain the process that occurs after fertilization in the female reproductive system.','After fertilization, the zygote undergoes its first cell division while traveling down the fallopian tube. This process involves rapid mitotic divisions, leading to the formation of a ball of cells, which eventually implants into the uterine wall to begin development.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(52,2,'الوحدة العامة','الفصل العام','الدرس العام','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_146_diag_40.png','YES','The graph illustrates growth over time, which can be labeled and used to derive educational questions about growth rates and age-related changes.','What is Ahmed\'s height at the age of 6 years?','Approximately 110 cm.','At what age does Ahmed reach a height of approximately 150 cm?','{\"A\": \"12 years\", \"B\": \"9 years\", \"C\": \"15 years\", \"D\": \"18 years\"}','A','The graph shows that Ahmed\'s height reaches approximately 150 cm at the age of 12 years.','Explain how Ahmed\'s height changes from age 0 to age 18.','Ahmed\'s height generally increases with age, starting at approximately 50 cm at age 0 and reaching about 175 cm by age 18. The growth is relatively steady from ages 0 to 12, after which the rate of increase slows down slightly, indicating a typical growth pattern during childhood and adolescence.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(53,2,'الوحدة العامة','الفصل العام','الدرس العام','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_151_diag_41.png','YES','The illustration depicts a labeled atomic structure, including the nucleus and electrons, which is suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What are the two types of particles found in the nucleus of an atom?','Protons and neutrons.','How many electrons are shown in the diagram orbiting the nucleus?','{\"A\": \"5\", \"B\": \"7\", \"C\": \"12\", \"D\": \"10\"}','A','The diagram shows 5 red dots representing electrons orbiting the nucleus.','Explain the role of protons and neutrons in the nucleus of an atom.','Protons are positively charged particles that determine the atomic number and identity of an element, while neutrons are neutral particles that contribute to the mass of the atom and help stabilize the nucleus by offsetting the repulsive forces between protons.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(54,2,'الوحدة العامة','الفصل العام','الدرس العام','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_151_diag_42.png','YES','The diagram categorizes matter into solid, liquid, and gas with distinct labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What are the two types of particles found in the nucleus of an atom?','Protons and neutrons.','How many electrons are shown in the diagram orbiting the nucleus?','{\"A\": \"5\", \"B\": \"7\", \"C\": \"12\", \"D\": \"10\"}','A','The diagram clearly shows 5 red dots representing electrons orbiting the nucleus.','Explain the role of protons and neutrons in the nucleus of an atom.','Protons are positively charged particles that determine the atomic number and identity of an element, while neutrons are neutral particles that contribute to the mass of the atom and help stabilize the nucleus by offsetting the repulsive forces between protons.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(55,2,'الوحدة العامة','الفصل العام','الدرس العام','output_diagrams_sem2/diagram_page_153_diag_43.png','YES','The illustration presents a Venn diagram comparing two concepts related to carbon, which can be labeled and used for educational questions.','What are the two forms of carbon illustrated in the Venn diagram?','Diamond (ألماس) and graphite (الجرافيت).','How are the atoms arranged in diamond according to the diagram?','{\"A\": \"In layers\", \"B\": \"In cubic crystals\", \"C\": \"In a random pattern\", \"D\": \"In a hexagonal structure\"}','B','The diagram states that in diamond, atoms are arranged in the form of cubic crystals.','Explain the significance of the intersection in the Venn diagram.','The intersection of the Venn diagram indicates that both diamond and graphite are forms of carbon, highlighting their commonality despite their different atomic arrangements. This shows that different structures of the same element can lead to distinct physical properties.','2026-11-17 13:30:56'),(56,3,'الوحدة 5: النباتات وموارد البيئة','الفصل 9: النباتات','الدرس 2: النباتات البذرية','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_26_diag_01.png','YES','The illustration depicts a plant cell with distinct labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What is the function of the cuticle in a plant leaf?','The cuticle serves as a protective outer layer that prevents water loss from the leaf.','Which layer of the leaf is primarily responsible for photosynthesis?','{\"A\": \"الطبقة العمادية (Palisade Layer)\", \"B\": \"البشرة العلوية (Upper Epidermis)\", \"C\": \"الطبقة الإسفنجية (Spongy Layer)\", \"D\": \"البشرة السفلية (Lower Epidermis)\"}','A','The palisade layer contains elongated cells with numerous chloroplasts, making it the primary site for photosynthesis.','Explain how the structure of the spongy layer contributes to gas exchange in leaves.','The spongy layer consists of irregularly shaped cells with large air spaces between them, which allows for efficient gas exchange. This structure facilitates the movement of carbon dioxide into the leaf and oxygen out of the leaf, essential for photosynthesis and respiration.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(57,3,'الوحدة 5: النباتات وموارد البيئة','الفصل 10: موارد البيئة وحمايتها','الدرس 1: موارد البيئة','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_49_diag_02.png','YES','The illustration depicts a hydroelectric power system with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes and question derivation.','What type of energy is represented by the water stored behind the dam?','Potential energy of water.','What happens to the potential energy of water as it flows down from the dam?','{\"A\": \"It is converted into kinetic energy.\", \"B\": \"It is lost as heat.\", \"C\": \"It remains unchanged.\", \"D\": \"It is converted into chemical energy.\"}','A','As the water flows down from the dam, its potential energy is converted into kinetic energy, which is necessary for driving the turbine.','Explain how the kinetic energy of water is utilized in hydroelectric power generation.','In hydroelectric power generation, the kinetic energy of flowing water is harnessed to rotate a turbine. As water flows down from a height, it gains speed and kinetic energy. This kinetic energy is transferred to the turbine, causing it to spin. The spinning turbine is connected to a generator, which converts the mechanical energy into electrical energy, thus generating electricity.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(58,3,'الوحدة 5: النباتات وموارد البيئة','الفصل 10: موارد البيئة وحمايتها','الدرس 1: موارد البيئة','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_50_diag_03.png','YES','The illustration depicts a scientific mechanism related to energy generation with labeled components that can be identified and used for educational questions.','What is the primary energy source used in a nuclear power plant?','The primary energy source is nuclear energy derived from atomic reactions.','What process occurs after the thermal energy is generated in the nuclear power plant?','{\"A\": \"The steam is used to turn a turbine.\", \"B\": \"The water is cooled back into liquid.\", \"C\": \"Electricity is generated directly from the reactor.\", \"D\": \"The nuclear fuel is replaced.\"}','A','The steam generated from the thermal energy is used to turn a turbine, which is a crucial step in electricity generation.','Explain how nuclear energy is converted into electrical energy in a nuclear power plant.','Nuclear energy is first harnessed in the reactor vessel, where atomic reactions occur, producing heat. This heat is used to convert water into steam in a heat exchanger. The steam then drives a turbine, converting kinetic energy into mechanical energy. Finally, this mechanical energy is transformed into electrical energy through a generator connected to the turbine.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(59,3,'الوحدة 5: النباتات وموارد البيئة','الفصل 10: موارد البيئة وحمايتها','الدرس 1: موارد البيئة','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_52_diag_04.png','YES','The illustration depicts a scientific mechanism related to fluid dynamics, with distinct components that can be labeled and used for educational questions.','What is the primary function of the turbine in the tidal power generation system?','The primary function of the turbine is to convert the kinetic energy of flowing water into mechanical energy.','What does the red arrow in the diagram indicate?','{\"A\": \"The direction of water flow\", \"B\": \"The direction of wind flow\", \"C\": \"The path of electricity\", \"D\": \"The location of the turbine\"}','A','The red arrow indicates the direction of water flow through the conduit, which is essential for the operation of the turbine.','Explain how the tidal power generation system harnesses energy from water.','The tidal power generation system harnesses energy by utilizing the movement of water caused by tides. As water flows through the conduit, it spins the turbine, converting the kinetic energy of the moving water into mechanical energy. This mechanical energy can then be transformed into electrical energy using a generator, providing a renewable energy source.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(60,3,'الوحدة 5: النباتات وموارد البيئة','الفصل 10: موارد البيئة وحمايتها','الدرس 2: التلوث وحماية البيئة','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_58_diag_06.png','YES','The illustration depicts the greenhouse effect with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes and question derivation.','What is the role of greenhouse gases in the Earth\'s atmosphere?','Greenhouse gases trap heat near the Earth\'s surface, preventing it from escaping into space.','What do the red arrows in the diagram represent?','{\"A\": \"Heat trapping near the Earth\'s surface\", \"B\": \"Sunlight entering the atmosphere\", \"C\": \"Energy escaping into space\", \"D\": \"Greenhouse gases in the atmosphere\"}','A','The red arrows indicate the re-emission of energy that is trapped and reflected back towards the Earth by greenhouse gases.','Explain how the greenhouse effect is similar to a physical greenhouse.','The greenhouse effect is similar to a physical greenhouse because both structures allow sunlight to enter but trap heat. In a greenhouse, sunlight warms the plants and the air inside, while the glass prevents heat from escaping. Similarly, greenhouse gases in the atmosphere let sunlight in but trap some of the heat that is re-emitted from the Earth\'s surface, maintaining a warmer temperature on Earth.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(61,3,'الوحدة 5: النباتات وموارد البيئة','الفصل 10: موارد البيئة وحمايتها','الدرس 2: التلوث وحماية البيئة','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_59_diag_07.png','YES','The illustration depicts molecular structures and layers of the Earth, which are relevant for 8th-grade science and can be labeled and used for educational questions.','What are the main layers of Earth\'s atmosphere as depicted in the diagram?','The main layers are: الأرض (Earth), طبقة التروبوسفير (Troposphere), طبقة الستراتوسفير (Stratosphere), الأوزون (Ozone), and طبقة الميزوسفير (Mesosphere).','Which molecule is represented as having three atoms bonded together in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Ozone molecule\", \"B\": \"Oxygen molecule\", \"C\": \"Carbon dioxide molecule\", \"D\": \"Nitrogen molecule\"}','A','The ozone molecule is depicted with three red spherical atoms bonded together, distinguishing it from the oxygen molecule, which has two.','Explain the significance of the ozone layer in Earth\'s atmosphere.','The ozone layer is crucial for life on Earth as it absorbs the majority of the sun\'s harmful ultraviolet (UV) radiation. This protection helps prevent skin cancer and other health issues in humans and preserves ecosystems.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(62,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 11: الطاقة الحرارية','الدرس 1: درجة الحرارة','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_84_diag_10.png','YES','The illustration depicts a thermometer with distinct labeled components and temperature scales, making it suitable for educational purposes in understanding temperature measurement.','What is the boiling point of water in Celsius?','100°C','What is the freezing point of water on the Kelvin scale?','{\"A\": \"273.15 K\", \"B\": \"373.15 K\", \"C\": \"0 K\", \"D\": \"-273.15 K\"}','A','273.15 K is the correct freezing point of water, as indicated on the Kelvin thermometer in the diagram.','Explain why absolute zero is significant in temperature scales.','Absolute zero is the theoretical temperature at which all molecular motion ceases, representing the lowest limit of the thermodynamic temperature scale. It is significant because it serves as a reference point for the Kelvin scale, indicating the point at which a substance has minimum thermal energy.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(63,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 11: الطاقة الحرارية','الدرس 3: المحركات والثلاجات','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_94_diag_11.png','YES','The illustration depicts a labeled diagram of an engine component, which is suitable for educational purposes in understanding mechanical systems.','What is the function of the fuel injector in an internal combustion engine?','The fuel injector sprays fuel or an air-fuel mixture into the combustion chamber.','Which component is responsible for injecting fuel into the cylinder?','{\"A\": \"صمام الحقن (Injection Valve)\", \"B\": \"المكبس (Piston)\", \"C\": \"الأسطوانة (Cylinder)\", \"D\": \"حاقن الوقود (Fuel Injector)\"}','D','The حاقن الوقود (Fuel Injector) is specifically designed to inject fuel into the combustion chamber.','Explain how the movement of the piston affects the combustion process in a four-stroke engine.','In a four-stroke engine, the downward movement of the piston creates a vacuum that draws in the air-fuel mixture through the open valves. This mixture is then compressed as the piston moves back up, leading to ignition and combustion when the spark plug fires. The piston’s movement is crucial for the intake and compression strokes, directly influencing the efficiency of the combustion process.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(64,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 11: الطاقة الحرارية','الدرس 3: المحركات والثلاجات','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_94_diag_12.png','YES','The illustration depicts a labeled diagram of an engine component, which is suitable for educational purposes in understanding mechanical systems.','What is the function of the fuel injector in an internal combustion engine?','The fuel injector sprays fuel or an air-fuel mixture into the combustion chamber.','What component is responsible for injecting fuel into the cylinder?','{\"A\": \"Fuel Injector\", \"B\": \"Piston\", \"C\": \"Cylinder\", \"D\": \"Intake Valve\"}','A','The fuel injector is specifically designed to inject fuel into the combustion chamber, as shown in the diagram.','Explain how the piston movement affects the combustion process in a four-stroke engine.','In a four-stroke engine, the piston moves down during the intake stroke, creating a vacuum that draws in the air-fuel mixture. This mixture is then compressed by the upward movement of the piston during the compression stroke, leading to combustion when ignited. The movement of the piston is crucial for the intake and compression phases of the engine cycle.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(65,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 11: الطاقة الحرارية','الدرس 3: المحركات والثلاجات','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_94_diag_13.png','YES','The illustration depicts a mechanical component with distinct labeled parts, making it suitable for educational purposes in understanding engine mechanisms.','What is the function of the fuel injector in an internal combustion engine?','The fuel injector sprays fuel or an air-fuel mixture into the combustion chamber.','Which component is responsible for injecting fuel into the cylinder?','{\"A\": \"Fuel Injector\", \"B\": \"Piston\", \"C\": \"Cylinder\", \"D\": \"Exhaust Valve\"}','A','The fuel injector is specifically designed to spray fuel into the combustion chamber, as indicated in the diagram.','Explain how the piston movement affects the intake of fuel in a four-stroke engine cycle.','During the intake stroke of a four-stroke engine, the piston moves downward, creating a vacuum that allows the fuel injector to spray fuel into the cylinder. This movement is crucial for drawing in the air-fuel mixture needed for combustion in the next stroke.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(66,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 11: الطاقة الحرارية','الدرس 3: المحركات والثلاجات','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_95_diag_14.png','YES','The illustration depicts a cooling system with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes and question derivation.','What is the function of the compressor pump in a refrigeration system?','The compressor pump circulates and compresses the refrigerant within the refrigeration system.','Which component in the refrigeration system is responsible for controlling the flow of refrigerant?','{\"A\": \"صمام التمدد (Expansion Valve)\", \"B\": \"مضخة ضاغطة (Compressor Pump)\", \"C\": \"ملفات التكثيف (Condenser Coils)\", \"D\": \"وحدة التجميد (Freezing Unit)\"}','A','The صمام التمدد (Expansion Valve) regulates the flow of refrigerant, allowing it to expand and cool before entering the freezing unit.','How does the refrigeration system expel heat from the cooling compartment?','The refrigeration system expels heat by circulating refrigerant through the condenser coils, where it releases heat to the outside environment. As the refrigerant passes through the coils, it changes from a gas to a liquid, effectively removing heat from the cooling compartment and maintaining a low temperature inside.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(67,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 1: الموجات','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_109_diag_16.png','YES','The illustration depicts a scientific concept related to wave motion with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes.','What type of wave is illustrated in the diagram?','The diagram illustrates a longitudinal wave.','What do the smaller red arrows labeled \'حركة ملفات النابض\' represent in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"The movement of the spring coils parallel to the wave direction\", \"B\": \"The direction of wave propagation\", \"C\": \"The regions of compression\", \"D\": \"The regions of rarefaction\"}','A','The smaller red arrows indicate the oscillation of the spring coils, which occurs parallel to the direction of wave propagation.','Explain how compressions and rarefactions contribute to the propagation of a longitudinal wave.','In a longitudinal wave, compressions are regions where particles of the medium are close together, resulting in higher pressure and density. Rarefactions are regions where particles are spread apart, leading to lower pressure and density. As the wave travels, these alternating regions of compression and rarefaction move through the medium, allowing the energy of the wave to propagate while the individual particles oscillate back and forth in place.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(68,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 1: الموجات','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_110_diag_17.png','YES','The illustration depicts a wave with labeled components (amplitude and wavelength), making it suitable for educational purposes in understanding wave properties.','What is the definition of wavelength in a transverse wave?','Wavelength in a transverse wave is the distance between two consecutive crests or troughs.','In the diagram, how is the wavelength of a transverse wave measured?','{\"A\": \"Distance between two consecutive crests\", \"B\": \"Distance between two consecutive compressions\", \"C\": \"Distance between two consecutive rarefactions\", \"D\": \"Distance between two hands holding the wave\"}','A','The wavelength of a transverse wave is measured as the distance between two consecutive crests, as indicated in the diagram.','Explain how the wavelength of a longitudinal wave differs from that of a transverse wave.','The wavelength of a longitudinal wave is measured from the center of one compression to the center of the next compression, while in a transverse wave, it is measured from crest to crest or trough to trough. This difference arises because longitudinal waves involve compressions and rarefactions, whereas transverse waves involve peaks and valleys.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(69,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 1: الموجات','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_111_diag_18.png','YES','The illustration depicts wave patterns with distinct features that can be labeled and used to formulate educational questions about wave properties.','What does the amplitude of a longitudinal wave depend on?','The amplitude of a longitudinal wave depends on the density of the medium in which compression and rarefaction occur.','Which spring represents a longitudinal wave with a larger amplitude?','{\"A\": \"The top spring\", \"B\": \"The bottom spring\", \"C\": \"Both springs have the same amplitude\", \"D\": \"Neither spring represents a longitudinal wave\"}','A','The top spring shows a more condensed area of coils, indicating a larger amplitude as stated in the diagram.','Explain how the amplitude of a longitudinal wave is visually represented in the diagram.','In the diagram, the amplitude of a longitudinal wave is visually represented by the degree of compression in the coils of the springs. A larger amplitude is shown by a more tightly packed area of coils, indicating greater compression, while a smaller amplitude is depicted by a less condensed area of coils, indicating lesser compression.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(70,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 1: الموجات','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_113_diag_19.png','YES','The illustration depicts the principles of reflection with labeled angles, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What is the law of reflection?','The law of reflection states that the angle of incidence is equal to the angle of reflection.','What is the angle labeled \'زاوية السقوط\' in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"The angle between the incoming light ray and the normal\", \"B\": \"The angle between the reflected light ray and the normal\", \"C\": \"The angle between the light source and the reflective surface\", \"D\": \"The angle between two incoming light rays\"}','A','The angle \'زاوية السقوط\' refers to the angle between the incoming light ray and the normal line, as depicted in the diagram.','Explain why the angle of incidence is equal to the angle of reflection.','The angle of incidence is equal to the angle of reflection due to the nature of light behavior when it strikes a reflective surface. This principle is based on the conservation of energy and the symmetrical properties of light waves, which dictate that the light will reflect off the surface at the same angle at which it arrived, relative to the normal line.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(71,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 2: موجات الصوت','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_115_diag_20.png','YES','The illustration depicts a molecular model with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in understanding concepts related to pressure and density.','What are the two regions of sound wave propagation illustrated in the diagram?','The two regions are compression (تضاغط) and rarefaction (تخلخل).','What does the red arrow in the diagram represent?','{\"A\": \"The movement of the drumhead when struck\", \"B\": \"The direction of sound wave propagation\", \"C\": \"The position of the air particles\", \"D\": \"The frequency of the sound wave\"}','A','The red arrow indicates the downward force or movement of the drumhead when it is struck, causing vibrations.','Explain how striking the drum creates sound waves in the air.','When the drumhead is struck, it vibrates, causing the air particles above it to move. This movement creates areas of compression where particles are closer together and areas of rarefaction where they are farther apart. These alternating regions of high and low pressure travel through the air as sound waves.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(72,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 2: موجات الصوت','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_115_diag_21.png','YES','The illustration depicts a molecular model with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in understanding pressure in gases.','What is the term used to describe the area where air particles are closer together in a sound wave?','Compression','What does the Arabic word \'تضاغط\' represent in the context of sound waves?','{\"A\": \"Compression\", \"B\": \"Rarefaction\", \"C\": \"Vibration\", \"D\": \"Frequency\"}','A','\'تضاغط\' translates to \'compression\', which refers to the area where air particles are closer together in a sound wave.','Explain how striking a drum creates sound waves in the air.','When a drum is struck, its membrane vibrates, creating areas of compression and rarefaction in the air. The downward force from the strike pushes air particles closer together, forming a compression. As the membrane returns to its original position, it creates a rarefaction where air particles are spread farther apart. This alternating pattern of compression and rarefaction propagates through the air as sound waves.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(73,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 3: الضوء','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_121_diag_22.png','YES','The illustration depicts a wave model with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in understanding wave properties.','What are the two components of an electromagnetic wave?','The two components of an electromagnetic wave are the electric field and the magnetic field.','Which field oscillates vertically in an electromagnetic wave?','{\"A\": \"Electric field (المجال الكهربائي)\", \"B\": \"Magnetic field (المجال المغناطيسي)\", \"C\": \"Both fields oscillate vertically\", \"D\": \"Neither field oscillates vertically\"}','A','The electric field (المجال الكهربائي) is represented by the blue sinusoidal wave and oscillates vertically, as indicated in the diagram.','Explain why the electric and magnetic fields in an electromagnetic wave are perpendicular to each other.','The electric and magnetic fields in an electromagnetic wave are perpendicular to each other due to the nature of electromagnetic radiation. As one field reaches its maximum, the other field also reaches its maximum, and when one field is zero, the other is also zero. This perpendicular relationship allows for the propagation of the wave through space, with both fields oscillating in a coordinated manner while being oriented at right angles to each other.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(74,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 3: الضوء','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_122_diag_23.png','YES','The illustration depicts wave patterns and their interactions, which are suitable for teaching concepts related to waves and energy in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What are the types of electromagnetic waves shown in the diagram?','The types of electromagnetic waves shown are Radio waves, Microwaves, Infrared waves, Visible light, Ultraviolet waves, X-rays, and Gamma rays.','Which direction indicates increasing wavelength in the electromagnetic spectrum?','{\"A\": \"Left\", \"B\": \"Right\", \"C\": \"Up\", \"D\": \"Down\"}','A','The left direction is labeled \'تزايد الطول الموجي\' (Increasing Wavelength), indicating that wavelength increases as you move left.','Explain how the frequency of electromagnetic waves changes across the spectrum.','As you move from left to right across the electromagnetic spectrum, the frequency of the waves increases. This is because waves on the left, such as Radio waves, have longer wavelengths and lower frequencies, while waves on the right, like Gamma rays, have shorter wavelengths and higher frequencies. This relationship is fundamental to understanding the properties of different types of electromagnetic radiation.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(75,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 3: الضوء','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_123_diag_24.png','YES','The illustration depicts a scientific curve with distinct labeled components that can be identified and used for educational questions.','What are the three main regions of the electromagnetic spectrum illustrated in the diagram?','The three main regions are Infrared, Visible, and Ultraviolet.','In which region of the electromagnetic spectrum does the intensity peak according to the graph?','{\"A\": \"Visible\", \"B\": \"Infrared\", \"C\": \"Ultraviolet\", \"D\": \"Radio Waves\"}','A','The graph shows that the intensity distribution peaks in the Visible region, specifically in the blue/green area.','Explain why the intensity of electromagnetic radiation is highest in the visible spectrum compared to infrared and ultraviolet.','The intensity of electromagnetic radiation is highest in the visible spectrum because this range corresponds to the wavelengths that are most efficiently emitted by many sources of light, such as the sun. The human eye is also adapted to detect these wavelengths, making them crucial for vision. In contrast, infrared radiation has longer wavelengths and lower energy, while ultraviolet radiation has shorter wavelengths and can be absorbed by the atmosphere, reducing its intensity at the surface.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(76,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 3: الضوء','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_124_diag_25.png','YES','The illustration is an anatomical diagram of the eye with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes and question derivation.','What is the first structure that light passes through when entering the human eye?','The cornea.','Which part of the eye is responsible for refracting light rays to focus them on the retina?','{\"A\": \"Lens\", \"B\": \"Pupil\", \"C\": \"Cornea\", \"D\": \"Retina\"}','A','The lens is responsible for refracting light rays, allowing them to converge on the retina.','Explain how the structure of the eye contributes to the formation of a clear image.','The eye\'s structure, including the cornea, pupil, and lens, works together to focus light rays onto the retina. The cornea bends the light as it enters, the pupil regulates the amount of light, and the lens fine-tunes the focus. This precise arrangement ensures that light converges at the focal point on the retina, where a clear image is formed.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(77,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 3: الضوء','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_125_diag_26.png','YES','The illustration depicts the anatomy of the eye with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes and question derivation.','What part of the eye is responsible for focusing light?','The lens is responsible for focusing light.','What does the label \'ضوء من مصدر بعيد\' indicate in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Light from a distant source\", \"B\": \"Light from a nearby source\", \"C\": \"Light being absorbed\", \"D\": \"Light being reflected\"}','A','The label \'ضوء من مصدر بعيد\' translates to \'light from a distant source\', indicating the type of light entering the eye.','How does the lens of the eye contribute to vision?','The lens of the eye refracts light rays that enter the eye, bending them so that they converge on the retina. This process allows the eye to focus on objects at various distances, enabling clear vision.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(78,3,'الوحدة 6: الطاقة الحرارية والموجات','الفصل 12: الموجات والصوت والضوء','الدرس 3: الضوء','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_125_diag_27.png','YES','The illustration depicts the anatomy of the eye with labeled components, making it suitable for educational purposes in an 8th-grade science curriculum.','What part of the eye is responsible for focusing light?','The lens is responsible for focusing light.','What does the label \'ضوء من مصدر بعيد\' indicate in the diagram?','{\"A\": \"Light from a distant source\", \"B\": \"Light from a nearby source\", \"C\": \"Light being absorbed\", \"D\": \"Light being reflected\"}','A','The label indicates that the light rays depicted are coming from a distant source, which is essential for understanding how the eye focuses on far objects.','How does the lens of the eye contribute to vision when observing distant objects?','The lens of the eye refracts (bends) the incoming parallel light rays from distant objects, allowing them to converge on the retina. This process ensures that the image is focused correctly, enabling clear vision of faraway objects.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(79,3,'الوحدة العامة','الفصل العام','الدرس العام','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_138_diag_28.png','YES','The illustration depicts a graph with labeled axes and a clear linear relationship, making it suitable for educational purposes and question derivation.','What is the speed represented by the line graph?','The speed is 10 km/h.','What distance is covered after 3 hours according to the graph?','{\"A\": \"30 km\", \"B\": \"20 km\", \"C\": \"40 km\", \"D\": \"50 km\"}','A','The graph shows that at 3 hours, the distance is 30 km, as indicated by the data points.','Explain the relationship between time and distance as shown in the graph.','The graph shows a linear relationship between time and distance, meaning that as time increases, distance increases at a constant rate. For every hour that passes, the distance increases by 10 km, indicating a constant speed of 10 km/h.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(80,3,'الوحدة العامة','الفصل العام','الدرس العام','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_139_diag_29.png','YES','The illustration presents a bar graph that effectively conveys quantitative data, making it suitable for labeling and generating educational questions.','What was the quantity of aluminum collected on Wednesday?','1.0 kg','Which day had the highest quantity of aluminum collected?','{\"A\": \"الاثنين (Monday)\", \"B\": \"الأربعاء (Wednesday)\", \"C\": \"الجمعة (Friday)\", \"D\": \"None of the above\"}','A','The bar for الاثنين (Monday) shows the highest quantity collected at 3.5 kg.','Explain why the quantity of aluminum collected on Friday is less than that collected on Monday.','The bar chart indicates that 2.0 kg of aluminum was collected on Friday, while 3.5 kg was collected on Monday. This suggests that more aluminum was available for collection or that more effort was made on Monday compared to Friday.','2026-11-17 13:33:24'),(81,3,'الوحدة العامة','الفصل العام','الدرس العام','output_diagrams_sem3/diagram_page_139_diag_30.png','YES','The pie chart effectively illustrates the composition of gases, which is suitable for teaching about atmospheric science and can be used for labeling and generating questions.','What was the quantity of aluminum collected on Friday?','2.0 kg','Which day had the highest quantity of aluminum collected?','{\"A\": \"الجمعة (Friday)\", \"B\": \"الأربعاء (Wednesday)\", \"C\": \"الاثنين (Monday)\", \"D\": \"None of the above\"}','C','The highest quantity of aluminum collected was on الاثنين (Monday) with 3.5 kg.','Explain why it is important to track the quantity of aluminum collected over the week.','Tracking the quantity of aluminum collected helps in understanding recycling efforts, assessing community participation, and planning for future collection activities. It also provides insights into trends in recycling behavior, which can inform educational campaigns to increase awareness and participation.','2026-11-17 13:33:24');
